{
  "case_id": "2021-21-954",
  "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (General Prelogar)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Secretary of Homeland Security exercised his statutory discretion to make a policy judgment. He found that the benefits of MPP were outweighed by its domestic, humanitarian, and foreign policy costs. Yet, the lower courts ordered DHS to reinstate MPP in perpetuity, requiring ongoing negotiations with Mexico to send thousands of non-citizens into its territory. That was error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: General, the -- below, you argued 1252(f)(1) and its limitation on who could impose injunctions here. And it seems as though you've abandoned that, but what should we do with that provision in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Is there any indication in connection with the '96 Act that anyone in Congress expected that if there were -- was not sufficient detention capacity, that hundreds of thousands of people would be just paroled into the United States without being lawfully admitted? Did anyone say that in Congress?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: I don't think that there was express history on that point, but Congress was focused on the detention issue, and it thought that the new expedited removal provisions that it had added to the statute at the same time would function to alleviate part of the strain on detention resources."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: If you had to detain everybody, could you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So that -- that -- that suggests the argument that you gave up on, and that was the argument that \"shall\" doesn't literally mean shall this instant. It means shall as best you can."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: Well, no. I -- I think \"shall\" properly interpreted means that we should use the detention capacity that we've been afforded here. I think that the argument"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: -- was that we have express statutory release authorities here, and we think that all of these releases are happening in conformance with the INA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I need to know this for this reason, that I -- I -- I think -- suppose we do exactly what you suggested we might do, \"may\" means may. Okay? End of the matter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think you look in the first instance to the agency action itself. And -- and, here, the October 29 termination decision was by its own terms a new agency action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have several questions. If you had sufficient detention capacity, could you still exercise your discretion to parole people into the United States?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "is the State Farm issue with respect to the October memo before us or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In considering significant public benefit, is it appropriate for the Secretary to consider the possibility of some people remaining in Mexico against the possibility of all the people for whom there is not detention capacity coming into the United States?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what \"significant public benefit\" means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0004-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the General said that the \"shall\" language has been in existence since the turn of the century and that in no time in American history has any administration followed your interpretation and attempted to detain every single illegal immigrant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Just deal -- just deal with the history involving 1182 and 1226(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Texas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Texas is bringing a garden variety or two garden variety APA claims, one of which are sort of the traditional arbitrary and capricious that I mentioned earlier during my opening."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0005-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STONE: I had two points, Your Honor. The first were the statutory points and the relationship between 1182 as a way of satisfying (b)(2)(A) and (b)(2)(C)'s sort of dual requirement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 117,
        "start": 117
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: So --so the questions I was pushing you on, how to interpret \"significant public benefit,\" I also alluded to the fact there are State Farm issues potentially that did the -- they have discretion, did they reasonably exercise their discretion and have they sufficiently explained their exercise of discretion, very similar to the State Farm opinion itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "166258bcddf0eccd8abdd6ff4bf0c6e3acab26758ee8bd852862e22bc75a7d1d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-166258bcddf0-0005-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 122,
        "start": 122
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The individuals who are returned under MPP need a place to live. They need work authorization. They need access to counsel. They need to be protected against predatory violence from gangs and cartels."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-21-954",
      "confidence": 0.0,
